 60NI    28SI(36AR,4PG):XUNDL-3        2008TO15                  ENSDF    202709
 60NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2027$          
 60NI c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2008To15:                          
 60NI2c  Phys. Rev. C 78, 054318 (2008)                                         
 60NI c  Compiled by S. Geraedts and B. Singh (McMaster); Dec 16, 2008          
 60NI c  Following three experiments were performed:                            
 60NI c  1. E({+36}Ar)=134 MeV at Argonne National lab, Gammasphere array       
 60NI2c  for |g-rays, 3|p |DE-E silicon strip telescope LUWUSIA for particle    
 60NI3c  detection and liquid scintillator neutron detector array NEUTRON SHELL 
 60NI4c  for neutrons.                                                          
 60NI c  2. E({+36}Ar)=148 MeV at Argonne National lab, Gammasphere array       
 60NI2c  for |g-rays, Microball and Silicon Wall for charged-particle           
 60NI3c  detection and 20 liquid scintillator neutron detectors                 
 60NI4c  for neutrons.                                                          
 60NI c  3. E({+36}Ar)=143 MeV at LBNL, Gammasphere array for |g-rays, Microball
 60NI2c  for charged-particle detection and scintillator detectors for neutrons.
 60NI3c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g(|q)(DCO), (particle)|g coin              
 60NI c  One of the above experiments also used Fragment Mass Analyzer.         
 60NI c  Comparisons with spherical shell-model calculations for low-spin       
 60NI2c  states and cranked Nilsson-Strutinsky calculations for high-spin       
 60NI3c  rotational states.                                                     
 60NI cG $ The DCO values correspond to angles of 30|' and 83|', with gate      
 60NI2cG on |DJ=2, quadrupole (E2) transition, unless otherwise stated.         
 60NI3cG DCO values for selected transitions were also obtained in 30|',53|'    
 60NI4cG and 53|',83|' geometries. For 30|', 83|' geometry following values     
 60NI5cG are expected:                                                          
 60NI cG $ For gates on |DJ=2 transitions, the expected values of DCO's are:    
 60NI2cG 1.0 for a |DJ=2, quadrupole transition, |?1.0 for a |DJ=0, dipole      
 60NI3cG transition and |?0.6 for a |DJ=1, dipole transition.                   
 60NI4cG For gates on |DJ=1, dipole transitions, expected values of DCO's are:  
 60NI5cG 1.0 for a |DJ=1, dipole transition and |<1.7 for |DJ=2, quadrupole     
 60NI6cG or for a |DJ=0, dipole transition. Deviations from above values are    
 60NI7cG indicative of mixed dipole+quadrupole (mainly M1+E2, rather than       
 60NI8cG unlikely E1+M2) transitions.                                           
 60NI cG E(X)$ Poor fit in the level scheme, deviates by more than 3|s's.       
 60NI2cG Possibly the energy uncertainty is underestimated. Doubling the        
 60NI3cG uncertainty of this |g ray gives a better overall fit.                 
 60NI cG E(Y)$ DCO value corresponds to gate on |DJ=1, dipole transition        
 60NI cG M(Z)$ |DJ=0, |D|p=no transition, expected to be mainly M1              
 60NI cG MR$ 2008To15 state that Rose-Brink convention was used for mixing      
 60NI2cG ratios. To be consistent with ENSDF policy of using Krane-Steffen      
 60NI3cG convention, all the signs of mixing ratios in 2008To15 have been       
 60NI4cG reversed                                                               
 60NI cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g's (by compilers). Normalized           
 60NI2cL |h{+2}=3.6 as compared to critical |h{+2}=1.3. 18 |g-ray energies      
 60NI3cL deviate from the fitted values by more than 3|s's: two by more than    
 60NI4cL 5|s's, six by 4 to 5|s's, and ten by 3 to 4|s's. Doubling the          
 60NI5cL uncertainties of these 16 |g rays gives a normalized |h{+2}=2.2        
 60NI CL BAND(A)$ |g cascade based on GS                                        
 60NI CL BAND(B)$ |DJ=1 structure based on 3671, 4+                             
 60NI CL BAND(C)$ |DJ=1 structure based on 3187, 3+                             
 60NI CL BAND(D)$Magnetic-dipole rotational band-1.                             
 60NI2cL Band based on 8044, 9- state.                                          
 60NI3cL Configuration=|p[(1f{-7/2}{+-1}(fp){+1}]~#|n[1g{-9/2}{+1}(fp){+3}]     
 60NI CL BAND(E)$Magnetic-dipole rotational band-2.                             
 60NI2cL Band based on 11255, 12+ state.                                        
 60NI3cL Configuration=|p[(1f{-7/2}{+-1}(fp){+1}]~#|n[1g{-9/2}{+2}(fp){+2}] or  
 60NI4cL |p[(1f{-7/2}{+-1}1g{-9/2}{+1}]~#|n[1g{-9/2}{+1}(fp){+3}]               
 60NI CL BAND(F)$Magnetic-dipole rotational band-3.                             
 60NI2cL Band based on 11225, (11+) state.                                      
 60NI3cL Configuration=|p[(1f{-7/2}{+-1}(fp){+1}]~#|n[1g{-9/2}{+2}(fp){+2}] or  
 60NI4cL |p[(1f{-7/2}{+-1}1g{-9/2}{+1}]~#|n[1g{-9/2}{+1}(fp){+3}]               
 60NI CL BAND(G)$Magnetic-dipole rotational band-4.                             
 60NI2cL Band based on 8485, 9- state.                                          
 60NI3cL Configuration=|p[(1f{-7/2}{+-1}(fp){+1}]~#|n[1g{-9/2}{+1}(fp){+3}]     
 60NI CL BAND(H)$ |DJ=2 band based on 11443, 13-.                               
 60NI2cL Configuration=|p[(1f{-7/2}{+-2}(fp){+2}]~#|n[1g{-9/2}{+1}(fp){+3}]     
 60NI CL BAND(h)$ |DJ=2 band based on 11120, 12-.                               
 60NI2cL Configuration=|p[(1f{-7/2}{+-2}(fp){+2}]~#|n[1g{-9/2}{+1}(fp){+3}]     
 60NI CL BAND(I)$ |DJ=2 band based on 13246, 13+                                
 60NI2cL Configuration=|p[(1f{-7/2}{+-3}(1g{-9/2}{+1}(fp){+2}]~#                
 60NI3cL |n[1g{-9/2}{+1}(fp){+3}]                                               
 60NI CL BAND(J)$ |DJ=2 band based on 9665, 10+.                                
